@baseUrl = https://localhost:7046/odata

### OData metadata (Customer, Order, OrderItem and Product entity sets)
GET {{baseUrl}}/$metadata
Accept: application/xml

### Customer directory
GET {{baseUrl}}/Customers?$select=CustomerId,Name,City,State,CountryCode&$orderby=Name&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Find customers in a city
GET {{baseUrl}}/Customers?$filter=contains(City,'Seattle')&$select=CustomerId,Name,City,State,CountryCode&$orderby=Name&$top=50
Accept: application/json

### Bill-to accounts
GET {{baseUrl}}/Customers?$filter=IsBillTo%20eq%20true&$select=CustomerId,Name,City,State,CountryCode&$orderby=Name&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Ship-to locations for a bill-to account
GET {{baseUrl}}/Customers?$filter=BillToId%20eq%2042&$select=CustomerId,Name,AddressLine1,City,State,PostalCode,BillToId&$expand=BillToCustomer($select=CustomerId,Name)&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Customer profile and nested order history
GET {{baseUrl}}/Customers(42)?$select=CustomerId,Name,AddressLine1,AddressLine2,City,State,PostalCode,CountryCode&$expand=Orders($select=SalesOrderGenerationId,OrderDate,StatusCode,SalesTotal,PriceTotal;$expand=OrderItems($select=SalesOrderLineGenerationId,LineId,ShipQty,StockQty,NonstockQty,Price,TaxAmount;$expand=Product($select=ProductId,Description,CatalogNumber,ProductStatusId)))
Accept: application/json

### Customers with orders on or after a date
GET {{baseUrl}}/Customers?$filter=Orders/any(o:o/OrderDate%20ge%202026-01-01)&$select=CustomerId,Name,City,State&$orderby=Name&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Orders billed to a customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/Orders?$filter=BillToId%20eq%2042&$select=SalesOrderGenerationId,SalesOrderId,GenerationId,OrderDate,StatusCode,SalesTotal&$orderby=OrderDate%20desc&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Orders shipping to a customer location
GET {{baseUrl}}/Orders?$filter=ShipToId%20eq%2042&$select=SalesOrderGenerationId,SalesOrderId,GenerationId,ShipToId,OrderDate,RequiredDate,ShipDate,StatusCode&$orderby=RequiredDate&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Orders placed in a date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/Orders?$filter=OrderDate%20ge%202026-01-01%20and%20OrderDate%20lt%202026-02-01&$select=SalesOrderGenerationId,OrderDate,StatusCode,SalesTotal,PriceTotal&$orderby=OrderDate%20desc&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Orders with a required date that have not shipped
GET {{baseUrl}}/Orders?$filter=ShipDate%20eq%20null%20and%20RequiredDate%20ne%20null&$select=SalesOrderGenerationId,SalesOrderId,OrderDate,RequiredDate,ShipToId,StatusCode&$orderby=RequiredDate&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Look up an order by invoice number
GET {{baseUrl}}/Orders?$filter=InvoiceNumber%20eq%2012345&$select=SalesOrderGenerationId,SalesOrderId,InvoiceNumber,OrderDate,ShipDate,StatusCode,SalesTotal&$top=20
Accept: application/json

### Look up orders using a customer purchase-order number
GET {{baseUrl}}/Orders?$filter=PoNumber%20eq%20'PO-12345'&$select=SalesOrderGenerationId,SalesOrderId,PoNumber,OrderDate,StatusCode,SalesTotal&$top=20
Accept: application/json

### One order generation with bill-to, ship-to, lines, and products
GET {{baseUrl}}/Orders('ORDER-GENERATION-ID')?$select=SalesOrderGenerationId,SalesOrderId,GenerationId,OrderDate,RequiredDate,ShipDate,StatusCode,InvoiceNumber,PoNumber,SalesTotal,PriceTotal&$expand=Customer($select=CustomerId,Name),ShipToCustomer($select=CustomerId,Name,City,State),OrderItems($select=SalesOrderLineGenerationId,LineId,ShipQty,StockQty,NonstockQty,Price,OriginalPrice,TaxAmount;$expand=Product($select=ProductId,Description,CatalogNumber,ProductStatusId))
Accept: application/json

### Product catalog
GET {{baseUrl}}/Products?$select=ProductId,Description,AlternateDescription,CatalogNumber,ProductStatusId&$orderby=Description&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Search products by catalog-number prefix
GET {{baseUrl}}/Products?$filter=startswith(CatalogNumber,'ABC')&$select=ProductId,Description,CatalogNumber,ProductStatusId&$orderby=CatalogNumber&$top=50
Accept: application/json

### Filter by a product-status ID (use a value defined by the business)
GET {{baseUrl}}/Products?$filter=ProductStatusId%20eq%201&$select=ProductId,Description,CatalogNumber,ProductStatusId&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Products with order-line history
GET {{baseUrl}}/Products?$filter=OrderItems/any()&$select=ProductId,Description,CatalogNumber&$expand=OrderItems($select=ShipQty,Price;$expand=Order($select=SalesOrderGenerationId,OrderDate,StatusCode))&$top=50
Accept: application/json

### Order lines with product and parent-order details
GET {{baseUrl}}/OrderItems?$select=SalesOrderLineGenerationId,LineId,ShipQty,StockQty,NonstockQty,Price,TaxAmount&$expand=Product($select=ProductId,Description,CatalogNumber),Order($select=SalesOrderGenerationId,OrderDate,StatusCode)&$top=100
Accept: application/json

### Customer count only
GET {{baseUrl}}/Customers?$count=true&$select=CustomerId&$top=0
Accept: application/json
